{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01370",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 7.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.52,
      "end_seconds": 13.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.38,
      "end_seconds": 26.53,
      "duration_seconds": 11.15,
      "text": "it's my throat closing up i thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone my neighbour said I should get it looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.17,
      "end_seconds": 28.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.25,
      "end_seconds": 34.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "It's been going on for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.33,
      "end_seconds": 41.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "understood is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.19,
      "end_seconds": 48.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.0,
      "end_seconds": 51.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.82,
      "end_seconds": 65.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.34,
      "text": "Swollen lips goes along with it, most of the time. Ah, uh, I've been feeling faint too, for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.67,
      "end_seconds": 66.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.83,
      "end_seconds": 74.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "So, the swollen lips? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.87,
      "end_seconds": 95.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "any recent illness or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.12,
      "end_seconds": 100.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "No, not a a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.26,
      "end_seconds": 106.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.15,
      "end_seconds": 112.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.48,
      "end_seconds": 119.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Alright, is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.92,
      "end_seconds": 123.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.72,
      "end_seconds": 141.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.06,
      "end_seconds": 144.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yes, asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.67,
      "end_seconds": 151.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Understood. Alright, asthma, that matches what I have here. Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.86,
      "end_seconds": 162.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, I had a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.51,
      "end_seconds": 166.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.36,
      "end_seconds": 181.34,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.99,
      "end_seconds": 190.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.49,
      "end_seconds": 195.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "It's Seretide inhaler, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.21,
      "end_seconds": 203.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.9,
      "end_seconds": 206.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.58,
      "end_seconds": 224.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "any inherited conditions that that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.12,
      "end_seconds": 231.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "yeah, um, my daughter has type 1 diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.55,
      "end_seconds": 234.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.28,
      "end_seconds": 248.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.17,
      "end_seconds": 276.45,
      "duration_seconds": 14.28,
      "text": "Okay: BMI works out to 31.9, height 166 centimetres, temp 36.8 degrees. And pressure 103 over 58, pulse is 101 beats a minute, weight 88 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.18,
      "end_seconds": 279.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.7,
      "end_seconds": 282.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "we'll go over that shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.98,
      "end_seconds": 288.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.44,
      "end_seconds": 292.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.3,
      "end_seconds": 314.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Your lips are swollen, you have hives, you are wheezing and your pressure is low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.06,
      "end_seconds": 337.41,
      "duration_seconds": 20.35,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards anaphylaxis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a severe allergic reaction, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.19,
      "end_seconds": 341.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.78,
      "end_seconds": 366.3,
      "duration_seconds": 21.52,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like anaphylaxis, but I'd like to confirm. Let's get monitoring, for anaphylaxis. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. What I'm giving you is adrenaline, 0.5 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for anaphylaxis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.7,
      "end_seconds": 370.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "So, how soon will it work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.6,
      "end_seconds": 384.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "lie flat with your legs raised, I am giving the injection now. I'd like you to see the emergency team as well, and I'll write the referral"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 386.17,
      "end_seconds": 390.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "So, uh, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.24,
      "end_seconds": 399.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.4,
      "end_seconds": 405.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Erm, uh, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}